  "notes": "Official cause_code/category are TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields, copied verbatim even though the narrative clearly attributes the issue to a legacy design/analysis deficiency (theme captures this). No component failed during the event (Section D: N/A) — this is a discovered unanalyzed design condition, not a hardware failure, so FailureMode nodes represent the logical/design defect chain rather than physical component breakdowns. TDAFWP asserted as backup because Section V states cooling 'is provided by' it and batteries/FLEX DG could support safe shutdown for hours — treated as stated-available capability, not mere design-basis narration. Previous similar LERs are for Unit 1 (same site, docket 390) and are emitted as stubs per instructions, using unit digit from the report exactly as stated."
